A||||3||Fformula88||Rear Brake caliper/parking brake stuck||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||02-12-2001||05:29 PM||||I just got done replacing the rear brakes, calipers and cables on the rear of the new 85 SE.  It all turned out well, expcept the left brake is stuck on and won't release.  The pads went on fine and everything seemed to hook up without a problem.  I haven't tightened the new e-brake cables yet, so there is plenty of slack there.  Did I get sold a bad caliper or is the loose brake cable the cause.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">      <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||02-12-2001||09:55 PM||||Did you install the P-brake lever correctly?  What about the return spring?  If the caliper installed correctly, you should have no "squeeze" whatsoever until the p-brake lever is "adjusted-up" by working the lever up and down several times.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||02-12-2001||10:06 PM||||Try loosing the bleeder screw, if fluid squirts out you have a bad brake hose on that side. Replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||02-13-2001||05:39 PM||||Thanks guys.  I had everything hooked up correctly.  Turned out to be the caliper.  I took it off and exchanged it.  Now everything works great!||||reg||1
